{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507019-chronicle-project-2","id":1507019,"title":"Chronicle Project 2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-30T21:25:58-07:00","id":1507019,"title":"Chronicle Project 2","content":"I'll try again after last time's feedback, let's see if this time it goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> What happened is that a sept of Black Furies moved temporarily from their Caern in order to attack a refinery, at first sight had no relation to Pentex or one of its subsidiaries, but when they sent scouts to the place, they felt the influence of the Wyrm inside so they decided to take action anyway, the problem is that the situation escalated and involved a battle against Wyrm agents, in general Fomori and Black Spiral Dancers, they managed to win, but many were injured and could not be moved , so they established a temporary rest camp.<br /> <br /> Taking advantage of the lull, one of the BF, an Athroun called Laura, decided to contact a kinfolk of the Glass Walkers, a hacker called Megan, she lives in the same city as Laura's sister, who knows nothing about Garous or Gaia, Laura asked Megan to keep an eye on her sister in case something go wrong, the two exchanged emails and in that she learned of a series of murders involving women and there were indications that it was caused by a Formori, although this is still inconclusive. Concerned about her sister Laura asks Megan to press the local sept to take some action, but this is beyond her capabilities, first that she does not have a high position within the sept, second that the city where she lives, Ashcity (fictional city), is divided.<br /> <br /> The city has a total of three Caerns, the first being the Caern that is in the western part, the Caern of the West, which Megan is part, composed of Glass Walkers; The second one, which is a multitribal Caern, is in the eastern part, the East Caern, composed of Glass Walkers and a pack of Shadow Lords, originally these two Caerns had good relations, but after the second one accepted the Shadow Lords the relationship between the two became awkard. There is still a third underground Caern hidden in the lower part of the city, naturally a Bone Gnawer Caern, but Megan doesn't know this Caern and therefore doesn't comment on it.<br /> <br /> Worried about her sister, Laura sends a pack of three Garou to investigate and perhaps pressure the Caern to take action on the case, she would go herself, but her leg was in pretty bad shape after being hit by a silver bullet. They arrived in the city, but they weren't well received, what happened was that 2 to 3 years ago a trio of Furies appeared in the city looking for shelter after traveling a lot, the reasons they didn't tell, the Caern of the east accepted to shelter them for a few days and in the meantime there was a slaughter with deaths on both sides, both blamed each other, but it ended without a fight, but since then, the East Caern has created a paranoia with the Black Furies in general. Unsuccessfully, the pack of Furies is forced to return, but one of them acted alone by sneaking into the city, a Ragbash, which has the potential to, in the worst case scenario, cause a conflict between septs, which in the current state of these Furies would be disastrous.<br /> <br /> At the same time, a pack (the PCs) was on its way to the city after a Fetish that, in theory, would be posing as one of the Garou. In this they get in touch with Megan and find the pack of Furies and agree to help in exchange for clues about the Fetish.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T17:49:56-07:00","id":1507246,"title":"","content":"It's very complex for a game setup. You might want to give something easier for the PC's first session just so they get a grap on their characters and setting before having them dive into this mayhem.<br /> <br /> Garou don't leave their Caerns unguarded, that's an excellent way to lose all your renown and everything you're supposed to guard. There should at least be a skeleton crew manning the defenses.<br /> <br /> Why would the Fury ask for a kinfolk of another tribe to look after her sister? Even Megan is a close ally, what reason does she have to be so worried?<br /> <br /> Another note is that Three Caerns around one city is a lot, they should all probably be Caerns of lesser power, and maybe consider putting one at a noteable distance, but still with a need to gravitate towards the city you want to use.<br /> <br /> A fetish that poses as a Garou is a slightly weird thing. What animates it and gives it sentience to walk around, and why does it hide as a Garou? Wouldn't it make more sense for it to be a rogue Spirit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T18:52:43-07:00","id":1507251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507019-chronicle-project-2?p=1507246#post1507246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very complex for a game setup. You might want to give something easier for the PC's first session just so they get a grap on their characters and setting before having them dive into this mayhem.<br /> <br /> Garou don't leave their Caerns unguarded, that's an excellent way to lose all your renown and everything you're supposed to guard. There should at least be a skeleton crew manning the defenses.<br /> <br /> Why would the Fury ask for a kinfolk of another tribe to look after her sister? Even Megan is a close ally, what reason does she have to be so worried?<br /> <br /> Another note is that Three Caerns around one city is a lot, they should all probably be Caerns of lesser power, and maybe consider putting one at a noteable distance, but still with a need to gravitate towards the city you want to use.<br /> <br /> A fetish that poses as a Garou is a slightly weird thing. What animates it and gives it sentience to walk around, and why does it hide as a Garou? Wouldn't it make more sense for it to be a rogue Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explaining this thing between Megan and Laura, is that Laura needed help and Megan was the only contact in town she had for that and oddly enough women tend to have this sense of unity, so it's as simple as that.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know it's a small territory for three caerns, but I couldn't figure out a way to explain the whole Garou presence without them being part of the same caern and I wanted to avoid the microverse stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the fetish part, look, this is for an acquaintance who is running a game and he gave me the information on how to make a connection with the PC adventure, the problem is that the explanation was a little confusing. Basically the party needs a fetish because of a scroll they got from an Ananasi, but to read it they need a specific fetish that no one knows how to make and maybe one is in town in the possession of a Garou.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T12:31:05-07:00","id":1507307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507019-chronicle-project-2?p=1507246#post1507246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fetish that poses as a Garou is a slightly weird thing. What animates it and gives it sentience to walk around, and why does it hide as a Garou? Wouldn't it make more sense for it to be a rogue Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite interesting, perhaps some form of animated kachina inhabited by a chameleon or crab spirit.<br /> <br /> Possibly a rare form of kami inhabiting a vessel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1507019-chronicle-project-2?p=1507251#post1507251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, I know it's a small territory for three caerns, but I couldn't figure out a way to explain the whole Garou presence without them being part of the same caern and I wanted to avoid the microverse stuff.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the usual caern geography however maybe as an anomaly they were all part of the same greater caern, split by time or disruption they now encircle the city that\u2019s sprung up in the middle of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 04-03-2023, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}